<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Alba</h1><p class="st-meta">1796 CE – 1796 CE · capital Alba</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A republic proclaimed for a few days in the Piedmontese town of Alba in 1796, the first Jacobin republic on Italian soil.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon's</a> army drove back the Piedmontese troops of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-sardinia">Kingdom of Sardinia</a> in April 1796, local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacobin-club">Jacobins</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ignazio-bonafous">Ignazio Bonafous</a> and the exiled publicist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giovanni-antonio-ranza">Giovanni Antonio Ranza</a> entered Alba and proclaimed a republic, hoping for French support for a revolution in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic planted a liberty tree and issued proclamations calling on the Piedmontese to rise, but it had no real institutions and relied on the presence of French troops. Its leaders hoped to spread the revolution to other towns of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> preferred to make peace with the king. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-cherasco">Armistice of Cherasco</a>, signed on 28 April 1796, returned Alba to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-sardinia">Kingdom of Sardinia</a>, and the republic disappeared after only a few days.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1796 CE – 1796 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.44%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1796 CE – 1796 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Alba</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Giovanni Antonio Ranza, Ignazio Bonafous</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Piedmontese, Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Alba Republic (1796)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1796&amp;focus=republic-of-alba" aria-label="Republic of Alba on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4871 598 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Alba lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5191 854L5140 827"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5140 827h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5191 854h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5191 854h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Alba. <a href="/atlas?year=1796&amp;focus=republic-of-alba">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
